# Ionic Movie App with Angular & Firebase

This is a Movie Management app built using **Ionic** with **Angular**. It allows users to register, log in using **Firebase Authentication**, and manage movies with **Firebase Realtime Database**. Users can add, update, delete, and view their favorite movies. Additionally, users have a profile page to manage their account information.

## Features
- **User Authentication** with Firebase Authentication (Login & Registration)
- **Movie CRUD** (Create, Read, Update, Delete) with Firebase Realtime Database
- **Profile Page** for managing user account information
- **Favorites System** for storing favorite movies

## Table of Contents
- [Installation](#installation)
- [Usage](#usage)
- [Project Structure](#project-structure)

## Installation

To get started with this project locally, follow these steps:

1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/karimamaaoui/ionic-movie-app.git
   Navigate to the project directory: cd ionic-movie-app
   Install dependencies: npm install
   Install Ionic CLI (if you don t have it installed) : npm install -g @ionic/cli
   Install Angular dependencies :  npm install @angular/fire firebase


Usage
Running the Application
To run the app locally, use the following command:

bash
Copier le code
ionic serve
This will start the application and you can access it in your browser at http://localhost:8100.

Using the App
Sign Up: Register a new user with an email and password.
Login: Log in with the credentials you used during registration.
Manage Movies: Add, update, or delete movies.
Favorites: Mark movies as favorites and view them.
Profile Page: View and edit your profile.
Authentication
This app uses Firebase Authentication for user login and registration.

Firebase Authentication Setup
Register your app in the Firebase Console.
Enable Email/Password Authentication in the Firebase Authentication section.
Add Firebase configuration to your app in src/environments/environment.ts:
typescript
Copier le code
export const environment = {
  production: false,
  firebaseConfig: {
    apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY',
    authDomain: 'YOUR_AUTH_DOMAIN',
    databaseURL: 'YOUR_DATABASE_URL',
    projectId: 'YOUR_PROJECT_ID',
    storageBucket: 'YOUR_STORAGE_BUCKET',
    messagingSenderId: 'YOUR_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID',
    appId: 'YOUR_APP_ID'
  }
};
Firebase Setup
To set up Firebase Realtime Database:

Create a new Firebase project on Firebase Console.
Add a Realtime Database to your Firebase project.
Set up Firebase rules for the database:
json
Copier le code
{
  "rules": {
    ".read": "auth != null",
    ".write": "auth != null"
  }
}
Enable Firebase Authentication with Email/Password.
Add Firebase SDK
Install Firebase SDK by running:

bash
Copier le code
npm install @angular/fire firebase
Configure Firebase in your src/environments/environment.ts with the Firebase credentials.

Project Structure
The app is structured as follows:

src/app/: Contains all the core logic and components for the app
### `movie/`
This folder contains movie-related components, services, and pages.

- **`movie-list/`**: Displays a list of movies and allows the user to interact with them.
  
- **`update-movie/`**: Allows users to update movie details.
 
### `auth/`
Contains components and services for user authentication.

- **`login/`**: Login page for existing users.
 
- **`register/`**: Registration page for new users.
 
- **`profile/`**: User profile page for managing account details.
 
### `services/`
Contains service classes that interact with Firebase for various operations like authentication, movie management, and more.

- **`movie.service.ts`**: Provides methods for creating, reading, updating, and deleting movies in the Firebase Realtime Database.
  
  Example methods:
  - `getMovies()`: Fetches the list of movies.
  - `getMovieById(id: string)`: Retrieves details of a movie by its ID.
  - `addMovie(movie: Movie)`: Adds a new movie to Firebase.
  - `updateMovie(id: string, movie: Movie)`: Updates movie details in Firebase.
  - `deleteMovie(id: string)`: Deletes a movie from Firebase.

- **`auth.service.ts`**: Handles user authentication using Firebase Authentication.
  - Methods include `login(email: string, password: string)`, `register(email: string, password: string)`, `logout()`, etc.



